  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shobai Miley Shikhi Activity (Everyone Learns Together)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Bangladesh):  Despite progress over the past decade, education services in Bangladesh remain neither inclusive nor equitable for children with disabilities. Schools often lack accessible materials, flexible curricula, and teachers trained in inclusive pedagogy. Children with disabilities, particularly girls, often face stigma that discourage their enrollment and participation in learning. Government counterparts frequently view  inclusion merely as ensuring access to school, rather than creating environments where all children can learn. With FY 2024 funds, in collaboration with the Government of Bangladesh, this activity will enhance learning opportunities for all primary school children by providing technical assistance on disability inclusion, and developing and implementing a comprehensive, scalable model for inclusive education in public schools. USAID will focus on building a sustainable model that provides inclusive education in public schools by addressing students&apos; diverse learning needs; training teachers in identifying, supporting, and teaching children with disabilities; and improving awareness of the value of inclusive education among parents, caregivers, and communities. The activity will partner with the Ministry of Primary and Mass Education to strengthen service delivery of inclusive education and create inclusive school environments for all primary school children. This activity aligns with the USAID Education Policy priority of ensuring that children, particularly the most marginalized and vulnerable, have increased access to safe, quality education. Funding for this activity contributes to the Basic Education ($2,073,462) earmark with Girls in Areas of Conflict ($1,783,627), and Private Sector Engagement ($207,346) attributions.</narrative>
  </description>
